id: pm-vcs-staging-byte-fixture
title: Guarantee a real byte mutation in the CDC staging regression
description: "The streaming staging regression writes literal byte 42 at random offset 400. With probability 1/256 the byte is already 42, so the operation is a no-op and the unstaged-change assertion fails even when staging is correct. Observed on Node 22 in PR 144 CI run 39919162579; the same test passed in the first full gate and in isolation."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:58:19.503Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T08:00:14.269Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Pin the mutation coordinate to 42 and replace it with its XOR inverse; reverting only the changed write-byte expression must fail the existing unstaged-change assertion. Production staging, safety bounds and coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
parent: pm-vcs-phase6stage
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T08:00:07.636Z",codex-agent,"Fixed only the test fixture: coordinate 400 starts as byte 42 and the later write uses edited[400] XOR 255, guaranteeing a real mutation while keeping the large random payload and streaming contracts. Behavioral revert proof: restore only the old literal-42 write with the controlled coordinate retained; the original unstaged-change assertion fails deterministically (exit 1). Exact fixed bytes restored, then pm test pm-vcs-staging-byte-fixture --run --progress passed 1/1 with no skips. Test typecheck and focused lint passed. Production staging code and all safety/coverage thresholds are unchanged; leaving this item open for orchestrator verification."
